1
00:00:00,501 --> 00:00:04,400
This is Gav-IL, the judging app for HackIllinois 2027.

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:08,154
A judge types their email, and gets a one-time code.

3
00:00:08,154 --> 00:00:09,093
No passwords.

4
00:00:09,095 --> 00:00:12,527
They type the six-digit code from the email, and tap Sign in.

5
00:00:13,085 --> 00:00:14,261
And they are signed in.

6
00:00:14,387 --> 00:00:18,005
Then check-in shows each judge who they are, which Path they judge

7
00:00:18,005 --> 00:00:19,979
and the teams they won't be sent to.

8
00:00:19,982 --> 00:00:22,862
Below that, a short guide to how tonight works.

9
00:00:22,864 --> 00:00:24,976
Looks right sends the judge to their room.

10
00:00:25,524 --> 00:00:30,636
Then a signpost points to the first table, A12, and names the team to look for.

11
00:00:30,637 --> 00:00:32,797
The floor plan shows where that table is.

12
00:00:33,368 --> 00:00:36,776
And the clock at the top counts down the time left to judge.

13
00:00:37,282 --> 00:00:40,834
At the table, the judge types the code printed on the placard.

14
00:00:41,329 --> 00:00:45,457
At the wrong table, Gav-IL says right away where the team really is.

15
00:00:46,391 --> 00:00:50,211
The right table code, plus the two characters after the dot

16
00:00:50,211 --> 00:00:52,607
confirms it: right table, right team.

17
00:00:52,611 --> 00:00:55,215
Table talk can take notes while the team demos

18
00:00:55,215 --> 00:00:57,819
but only after everyone at the table says yes.

19
00:00:57,821 --> 00:01:02,113
The sheet gives the judge a line to read out loud, and says who gets what.

20
00:01:02,113 --> 00:01:03,389
The audio is not kept.

21
00:01:05,091 --> 00:01:07,342
While the team talks, the phone listens

22
00:01:07,342 --> 00:01:09,939
and the judge can mark a moment with one tap.

23
00:01:10,450 --> 00:01:13,468
When they stop, Gav-IL pulls out the highlights.

24
00:01:13,468 --> 00:01:14,914
It takes a few seconds.

25
00:01:14,914 --> 00:01:18,658
The judge keeps the highlights that are right, and they go into the notes.

26
00:01:18,660 --> 00:01:21,276
Next, the judge marks how the demo went.

27
00:01:21,279 --> 00:01:24,591
Then adds a private note, one that only they can see.

28
00:01:24,813 --> 00:01:28,029
If the project stands out, they nominate it for a prize.

29
00:01:28,030 --> 00:01:29,902
Then they submit.

30
00:01:30,167 --> 00:01:34,271
The evaluation is saved, and the app points them to the next table.

31
00:01:34,273 --> 00:01:37,042
At the next table, it is the same placard check.

32
00:01:37,042 --> 00:01:40,273
The judge types the code, and the app confirms the team.

33
00:01:41,653 --> 00:01:43,497
This team says no to recording.

34
00:01:43,497 --> 00:01:47,125
The judge taps Not this time, and it does not affect judging.

35
00:01:47,125 --> 00:01:51,157
The judge picks how the demo went, and types a short note to remember it.

36
00:01:51,814 --> 00:01:53,452
Then they submit.

37
00:01:53,667 --> 00:01:56,756
The app opens the comparison of the last two projects.

38
00:01:56,756 --> 00:01:59,787
Recall rows bring back what they noted at each table.

39
00:01:59,856 --> 00:02:02,712
They pick the stronger project, then tap Confirm.

40
00:02:02,882 --> 00:02:07,274
A pick can be undone for a few seconds, and the Undo button counts down.

41
00:02:08,081 --> 00:02:10,745
When the count runs out, the vote is sent.

42
00:02:11,050 --> 00:02:14,602
Then the app moves the judge on to the next table, PocketLab.

43
00:02:14,604 --> 00:02:18,972
Since EcoLens said no, the judge can still dictate a memo while they walk.

44
00:02:19,142 --> 00:02:20,617
Then they open My notes.

45
00:02:20,774 --> 00:02:24,590
Everything they wrote, and every highlight they kept, stays here.

46
00:02:24,591 --> 00:02:26,403
Only the judge sees them.

47
00:02:26,403 --> 00:02:31,839
That is Gav-IL on a judge's phone: sign in, judge, compare, and keep notes.
